From: Europa Sysop
To: All
Subj: The prototype that started it all
Date: 07-02-88 22:30

People keep asking about the machine The Pit ran on in 1987, so here it
is, as much as I can say.

It was an engineering sample of what became the ARM/AT.  The board was
marked REV X2 in hand lettering and the serial number sticker said
00017.  There were four wires soldered across the back of the board by
somebody in a hurry, a sticker on the case that said DO NOT SHIP, and a
second sticker, in different handwriting, that said SERIOUSLY.

A friend in the lab lent it to me "for testing".  A friend who still
can't talk about it, so please don't ask who.  I tested it by running a
bulletin board on it for eight months, which I maintain is a very
thorough test.

It went back when the production machines shipped.  I kept the keyboard.
Nobody has asked for it.  I type on it every night.

-- Europa
