@@6
From: Karen Whitfield
To: Maria Delgado
Subj: Re: EGA or VGA?
Date: 09-14-88 22:20

> Karen, want to take this one before I make something up?

Happily.

EGA: 640 x 350 in 16 colours, chosen from a palette of 64.  Crisp text,
fine for spreadsheets and most games.

VGA: 640 x 480 in 16 colours, chosen from 262,144.  And the one everyone
gets excited about: 320 x 200 with 256 colours on screen at once.  Needs
an analog monitor, so budget for one.

If the customer ever wants to play a game, or look at a fractal, or
has eyes, sell them the VGA.

KW
@@7
From: Susan Oyelaran
To: Karen Whitfield
Subj: Re: EGA or VGA?
Date: 09-15-88 07:30

> 320 x 200 with 256 colours on screen at once.

And on our machines, that mode (13h) is just 64,000 bytes starting at
address 0xA0000, one byte per pixel, row after row.  No planes, no
segments, no bank switching.  Pixel (x,y) is at 0xA0000 + y*320 + x.
A pointer and a STRB.  It's almost too easy.

Susan
... 16 registers and no segments: I'm home.
