From: Bill Tran
To: All
Subj: Modem init string help
Date: 10-24-89 00:48

My new 2400 keeps answering the phone when my grandmother calls.  She
thinks we have a fax machine now.  What do I put in the init string?
@@11
From: Europa Sysop
To: Bill Tran
Subj: Re: Modem init string help
Date: 10-24-89 08:15

> My new 2400 keeps answering the phone

Put S0=0 in your init string (auto-answer off).  S0=1 means "answer on
the first ring".  TERM sends AT&C1&D2 after ATZ by default, so the modem
also tells the computer when there is a carrier (&C1) and hangs up when
you drop DTR (&D2).  Alt-S in TERM to change it.

And tell grandma the screeching is the future.
