From: Marcus Feld
To: All
Subj: Sound card: which IRQ?
Date: 06-22-90 17:30

Got a Sound Blaster for my birthday!!!  (Thanks Grandma, and no, it is
not "a very loud modem".)  The box says set it to IRQ 5.  The ARM/AT
manual says something about IRQ 7.  Who do I believe?
@@21
From: Karen Whitfield
To: Marcus Feld
Subj: Re: Sound card: which IRQ?
Date: 06-22-90 21:05

> Who do I believe?

The ARM/AT manual.  On our machines, IRQ 5 and IRQ 6 share their
vectors with two of the ARM's own exception vectors, so the sound card
goes on IRQ 7, port 220h.  The games and drivers for the ARM/AT expect
it there.  (The printer port is also on 7 on paper, but nobody uses the
printer interrupt.  Nobody.)

Happy birthday.  Please keep the volume below "neighbours".

KW
